---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { AUTHOR } from "../site.config.js";
import { breadcrumbSchema, personRef } from "../lib/schema.js";

const crumbs = [{ name: "About", path: "/about/" }];
const schema = [breadcrumbSchema(crumbs)];
---

<Base
  title="About Our Engineering & Editorial Team"
  description="Learn about Eren Şimşir and the engineering methodology behind our transparent, open-formula wage and payroll calculation tools."
  schema={schema}
  crumbs={crumbs}
>
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12 lg:py-16">
    <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 p-8 sm:p-12 shadow-sm mb-12">
      <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center sm:items-start gap-6 pb-8 mb-8 border-b border-slate-200">
        <div class="w-24 h-24 rounded-2xl bg-gradient-to-br from-brand-600 to-brand-800 text-white flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-3xl shadow-md shrink-0">
          EŞ
        </div>
        <div>
          <span class="inline-flex items-center px-2.5 py-0.5 rounded-full text-xs font-semibold bg-brand-50 text-brand-700 border border-brand-200 mb-2">
            Founder & Lead Engineer
          </span>
          <h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold text-slate-900">{AUTHOR.name}</h1>
          <p class="text-sm text-brand-700 font-medium">{AUTHOR.role}</p>
          <div class="mt-3 flex items-center space-x-4 text-xs">
            <a href={AUTHOR.linkedin} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-slate-600 hover:text-slate-900 underline">LinkedIn Profile</a>
            <a href={AUTHOR.github} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-slate-600 hover:text-slate-900 underline">GitHub Repositories</a>
            <a href={`/author/${AUTHOR.slug}/`} class="text-brand-600 hover:text-brand-800 font-semibold">Full Author Bio &rarr;</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none text-sm text-slate-700 leading-relaxed space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">Mission & Technical Background</h2>
        <p>
          {AUTHOR.shortBio}
        </p>
        <p>
          Many online paycheck and wage calculators are opaque "black boxes" that fail to account for modern labor law complexities—such as non-discretionary bonus regular rate adjustments under FLSA § 7(e), statutory overtime calculations, or local state bracket nuances.
        </p>
        <p>
          Our aim is to explain wage and payroll rules with <strong>transparent, worked formulas</strong> and to point to the statute, regulation, or IRS publication behind each explanation. The calculators run in your browser and do not send the wage figures you enter to our servers.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 mt-8">Engineering Principles</h2>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
          <li><strong>Zero Server Data Collection:</strong> All wage and tax computations execute in your local browser using Vanilla JavaScript. Your financial details never touch a server.</li>
          <li><strong>Sourced Figures:</strong> Tax thresholds, wage bases, and wage rules come from the IRS, Department of Labor, and state publications linked at the end of each article. They change every year, so each article says which year its figures reflect.</li>
          <li><strong>Clear Attribution:</strong> When local municipal or collective bargaining agreements supersede federal baselines, we provide explicit citations and contextual guidance.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
